To pass HTTP headers into gRPC metadata using grpc-gateway, you use the runtime.WithMetadata option when initializing your ServeMux. This option registers a custom header matcher function that inspects incoming HTTP headers and decides which ones to forward to the gRPC context as metadata.

By default, grpc-gateway prefixes forwarded headers with grpcgateway- unless you explicitly handle them in a custom matcher.

Step-by-Step Implementation
1. Define the Custom Header Matcher
Write a function with the signature func(string) (string, bool) to filter and transform HTTP header keys.

