Thanks for the report, and for the analysis @Sagar07Kr. The cause is right. #45333 changed the user's Admin Events tab to filter on `users/<id>*`. Bulk removal goes through `ui-ext/role-mapping-delete/users/<id>`, and `RoleMappingDeleteResource` uses the request URI as the event's resource path, so the filter never matches it. Adding roles goes through `RoleMapperResource`, which logs `users/<id>/role-mappings/...`, and that's why additions show up.

This is closely related to #53747. Its PR, #53764, removes the `ui-ext` role-mapping endpoints, `RoleMappingDeleteResource` included, and switches the Admin Console to the Admin API. Removals would then go through the standard role-mappings endpoints and log the same resource paths as additions.

@pedroigor, this is your area, so I'll hand it over to you: whether #53764 covers this, whether 26.x needs a separate fix, and who should pick it up.
